title: The Paradigm Renaissance — ambient agents, intrinsic learning, and the orchestration protocol
summary: 'A philosophical inflection point for Paradigm. Through extended dialogue, arrived at a fundamentally new model for AI agent orchestration: agents as ambient team participants who self-select based on expertise, intrinsically drive their own learning, and operate through a standardized protocol analogous to what MCP did for tool use. This reframes Paradigm from a context engineering framework into the substrate for multi-agent collaboration — the HTTP moment for orchestration.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#paradigm'
  - '#symphony'
  - '#lore-loader'
  - '#agents-registry'
  - '#conductor'
decisions:
  - id: ambient-not-dispatch
    decision: Agent orchestration should be ambient attention, not top-down task dispatch
    rationale: Real teams don't have managers explicitly assigning every task. Team members listen, self-select, and speak up based on expertise. AI agent teams should work the same way.
  - id: intrinsic-learning
    decision: Learning should be an intrinsic agent trait, not framework-enforced compliance
    rationale: Stop hooks and habit checks are training wheels. The real model is agents that want to learn because getting better is their core drive. The framework provides substrate, not motivation.
  - id: lore-splits-three
    decision: Lore should split into work log, learning journal, and team decisions
    rationale: These serve different audiences (project, self, team), have different lifecycles (ephemeral, durable, institutional), and want to flow to different places.
  - id: orchestration-protocol
    decision: Define a standardized orchestration protocol (Agent Manifest, Orchestration Contract, Coordination Wire)
    rationale: MCP standardized agent-tool interaction. Nothing standardizes agent-agent-human interaction. This protocol is what makes an open agent marketplace possible.
  - id: symbols-as-attention
    decision: The 5 symbols become attention triggers for ambient agent participation
    rationale: When conversation touches ^gates, the security agent's attention fires. Symbols aren't just documentation — they're the signal layer for agent relevance filtering.
